  "text": "The Mabinogion is a set of Welsh mythological texts. Much of what we know of Welsh mythology comes from its four branches. Eight more tales sometimes count as part of the collection. Two manuscripts hold the stories: the White Book of Rhydderch (1300-1325) and the Red Book of Hergest (1375-1425). The tales were written after Christianization but draw on earlier oral literature, so they open a window on the Celtic past. Lady Charlotte Guest gave the first English translation in 1838-49. The name Mabinogion is the plural of the Middle Welsh word mabinogi. Specialists prefer the singular mabinogi today. The tales concern the Children of Dôn, who parallel the Irish Tuatha Dé Danann. The first branch follows Pwyll of Dyfed. The second recounts the journey of Brân the Blessed to Ireland. The third tells of Manawydan and Pryderi. The fourth deals with King Math and the hero Gwydion.",
